From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 22:07:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03351/11362] [outer-loop] arc: Go-Explore alone REFUTED for
 the hard tail (0/4) -- needs a goal gradient

Affordance-priored Go-Explore (budget 4000) reaches 0/4 hard-tail first-wins (ls20/su15/sk48/cn04)
despite deep archives (90-565 cells, maxdepth 160). It finds easy/shallow wins (r11l @8) but not the
deep NARROW specific-sequence wins -- broad systematic coverage cannot hit a narrow 13-33-action win
with no intermediate reward and no gradient. Confirms the mechanic diagnosis: the hard tail needs a
sub-goal GRADIENT (LLM-as-reasoner: analyze grid -> hypothesize mechanic -> propose actions), the SOTA
layer ON TOP of the archive. Blind exploration (diversity + Go-Explore) is refuted for the hard tail;
the archive is reusable infrastructure for the LLM-guided version.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
